+### 1.8 A literal-only change that cannot be described — `patches/fixes/0006-literal-only-change-not-describable.patch`
+
+Also in the second patch group, and also a send to `#f`. A literal DirCtgy or GroupCtgy change is disallowed:
+`make-change-template` (`rules.ss:1060-1065`) removes the literal descriptor from the template's descriptor list.
+When the only descriptor was the literal one (a subobjects DirCtgy change with only a literal descriptor), the list
+is left empty. `instantiate-change-template` (`rules.ss:893-912`) then `stochastic-pick`s from `()`, which gives `#f` without
+drawing a random number, and `set-quality-values` reaches `compute-rule-abstractness` (`rules.ss:1609`), which sends
+`get-conceptual-depth` to it (`abcx -> xwva; ijkr`, seed 19, at codelet 8012: `rule-scout`, `Exception: attempt
+to apply non-procedure #f`).
+
+`rule-scout` already stops a rule whose objects cannot be described: `possible-to-instantiate?` (`rules.ss:445-458`)
+makes it fizzle with "Not all rule objects are describable", but it looked only at the objects, not at the changes.
+
+- **`possible-to-instantiate?`** now also needs, for every intrinsic clause template, a non-empty descriptor list in
+  each of its change templates: `(andmap (lambda (change-template) (pair? (3rd change-template))) (3rd template))`.
+  A template with an empty list is not describable, and `rule-scout` fizzles, as it does for an object it cannot describe.
+  It is the only caller of `instantiate-rule-clause-template` and so the only place the descriptor list is picked from.
+
+The patch is written on the line it replaces, so no line of `rules.ss` moves.
+
+**Effect on behaviour: none where it does not fire.** Every rule clause whose change templates all have a descriptor
+takes the same path as before, with the same random draws; the clause that is now refused ended the run in an error.
+Rejected: dropping the empty change (the rule then says less than the bridges did), filtering `#f` in
+`compute-rule-abstractness`, skipping it in `abstract-change-descriptions` (it changes the random stream), and
+allowing a literal DirCtgy change (it is disallowed on purpose).
+
